below. The structure check passed.\", \"mappings\": [\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-0cf58a00\", \"basis\": \"R10\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The validation matrix adds the required race check governance-read-view-integration over the B34 selection and explicit -count=1 checks, qualifying R10's fixtures and fault injection as V7 requires.\"},\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-5c5ba300\", \"basis\": \"D2\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The spec requires the B34 ADR to be accepted before the contract changes; the ADR records the bounded operation-scoped view and budgets on which D2-D9 rest.\"},\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-98ca1442\", \"basis\": \"D8\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"delegation.json is instance-only review-agent configuration, excluded from the embedded scaffold (distpolicy.go:115-118) per D8; its narrowed session capture responds to the retained capture failure. It contains no secrets.\"}\n    ]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-27c4d1637d54580e\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the new section in POSE.md:921-958, its pt-BR translation at locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:930-969 and both scaffold copies (dist/POSE.md:908-945, dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:930-969). The texts are equivalent across languages and the generated copies match their sources. The referenced commands exist (pose delegate watch at cli/delegate.go:223 and cli/help_catalog.go:360; wait, resume, handoff and agents are documented elsewhere in the manual). The guidance is consistent with the existing delegation contracts and declares no new mandatory layer. The read-view documentation (POSE.md:372-373) remains accurate.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-27c4d1637d54580e\", \"rationale\": \"The new guidance is actionable: follow runs with watch/wait, preserve failed and quota-limited attempts, persist derived inputs before a detached review, and check authentication and capture after setup failures. Runtime error remediation (index rerun/verify, guard refusals) is unchanged and actionable.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R1-R10 remain covered by the sealed B34 integration and the projection, writer and index checks on the current canonical validation (fc001153, 189/0); the editorial delta adds no requirement.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-27c4d1637d54580e\", \"rationale\": \"The post-close delta touches only the manuals and their generated copies (plus spec prose outside this change set). No requirement, artifact plan, runtime code or exit gate was expanded, and the plan's exclusions (no watcher, daemon or cache) still hold.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-27c4d1637d54580e\", \"rationale\": \"The editorial text discloses no secrets, paths or credentials, and its advice reinforces preserving independence and not bypassing provider limits. The security conclusions from round 2 still hold: lock-path link checks, explicit foreign-root bindings, digest-only roots, the bounded executable digest, and the delegation policy excluded from the scaffold.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-27c4d1637d54580e\", \"rationale\": \"The editorial addition is the smallest sufficient change: advisory prose within the existing workflow, explicitly not a new gate. The runtime design remains the bounded Files extension with no daemon or cache. That choice would be invalidated if real corpora exceeded the D6 budgets without a new measurement.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"check:artifact-check\", \"rationale\": \"Required tool with no evidence class; the reference is the primary execution's run of the command, per the native convention (review_bundle.go:2867-2875). I did not run it myself and did not inspect its output.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-27c4d1637d54580e\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed structural design result passes for this bundle.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; not executed in my restricted read-only session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"tests\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; not executed in my restricted read-only session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Cites a passing sealed integration record of the class the tool requires. The integration inventory itself is static, not functional proof, and the command was run by the primary execution, not by me.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; not executed by me. Its known limitation stands: INCOMPLETE because two historical specs cannot be read.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Post-review gate: has the review-complete precondition and runs after this conclusion is attested.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"knowledge-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"check:knowledge-check\", \"rationale\": \"Required tool with no evidence class; the reference is the primary execution's run of the command. I did not run it myself.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Post-review gate: has the review-complete precondition and evaluates the